            {
              "text": "Several law firms in the **Chermside** and **North Lakes** areas (and their immediate surrounding northern corridors) handle estate litigation, Family Provision Applications (FPAs), and contested wills.\n\n---\n\n### **1. North Lakes Law Firms**\n\n* **Cooke & Hutchinson Lawyers**\n  * **Location:** Level 1, Suite 205, North Lakes Central, 53 Endeavour Boulevard, North Lakes\n  * **Specialisation:** A boutique firm with over 40 years on the peninsula and northern corridor. Their Wills & Estates practice specifically lists **Estate Litigation** among its core services, including Family Provision claims, testamentary capacity challenges, undue influence disputes, statutory wills, and equitable/constructive trust claims.\n* **Turner Freeman Lawyers (North Lakes Branch)**\n  * **Location:** Suite 6, 2/25 Discovery Drive, North Lakes\n  * **Specialisation:** A national firm with a dedicated Wills & Estates litigation division. They frequently represent both applicants and executors in Family Provision Applications, claims involving unfair or unequal wills, and executor defense. They commonly offer “No Win, No Fee” assessments for eligible claimants.\n* **Zande Law**\n  * **Location:** Norwinn Centre, 15 Discovery Drive, North Lakes\n  * **Specialisation:** Long-established in North Lakes, Zande Law handles estate planning, deceased estate administration, and resolving contested will matters and inheritance disputes among family beneficiaries.\n* **Coastside Law**\n  * **Catchment:** Servicing North Lakes, Redcliffe, and the Moreton Bay corridor\n  * **Specialisation:** Focuses specifically on contesting wills and Family Provision claims involving blended families, superannuation/life insurance passing outside the will, and defending executors against claims.\n* **Brisbane Elder Law / QLD Estate Lawyers**\n  * **Location:** Norwinn Business Centre, 15 Discovery Drive, North Lakes\n  * **Specialisation:** Niche focus on estate litigation, will disputes, testamentary capacity assessments, undue influence challenges, and Family Provision claims.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Chermside (and Immediate Surrounds) Law Firms**\n\n* **Pennisi Zia Lawyers**\n  * **Location:** Chermside office (and Brisbane CBD)\n  * **Specialisation:** Acts extensively in estate litigation and disputed estates. They assist clients with Family Provision Applications (defending or pursuing claims), challenging wills on the grounds of undue influence or lack of capacity, and rectifying estate distributions.\n* **Terry Anderssen Lawyers**\n  * **Location:** 7/692 Gympie Road, Chermside\n  * **Specialisation:** A longstanding suburban firm on Gympie Road focusing heavily on wills, probate, letters of administration, and estate disputes/litigation across Brisbane’s Northside.\n* **A.L.F. Lawyers (Just North of Chermside in Strathpine)**\n  * **Location:** 8/427 Gympie Road, Strathpine (approx. 10 minutes from Chermside)\n  * **Specialisation:** Prominently handles estate disputes and contentious probate across North Brisbane. They represent both claimants making Family Provision Applications and executors tasked with defending the estate.\n* **Maurice Blackburn Lawyers (North Brisbane / North Lakes)**\n  * **Location:** North Lakes branch & servicing Chermside clients\n  * **Specialisation:** Major plaintiff litigation firm with a dedicated contested wills department. They handle FPAs, capacity claims, and elder financial abuse claims.\n\n---\n\n### **Important Notes for Contesting a Will in Queensland:**\n* **Strict Time Limits apply under the *Succession Act 1981* (Qld):**\n  * **6 Months:** You must give **written notice** of your intention to file a Family Provision claim to the executor within 6 months of the deceased’s death.\n  * **9 Months:** The formal court application must be filed within 9 months of the date of death.\n* **Eligibility:** In Queensland, only spouses (including de facto and civil partners), children (including biological, stepchildren, and adopted children), and dependants are eligible to file a Family Provision Application.",
